  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting livelihoods through ecotourism routes for forest and peace</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a third phase of a previous PACT funded intervention that aims at demonstrating the
potential of community-based ecotourism in biodiversity hotspots as a means to sustain rural
livelihoods, reduce deforestation, avoid GHG emissions and strengthen peace-building in two postconflict
regions (the Quinchas- Boyac&#xe1;, the Perij&#xe1;-Zapatosa region-Cesar ). This new phase will secure the
implementation of the ecotourism plans co-developed in Phase Two, using enhanced capacities and
knowledge of forest and marketing tools to pilot the ecotourism routes for forest and peace. Additionally
it will continue testing the community agreements to distribute the costs and benefits of new green
tourism economies.</narrative>
  </description>
